-2-KADGY7NO.svg" style=3D"color: transparent;"></div></figure>
<p>Rearranging elements around the pivot<br>
Let=E2=80=99s see if we can do this in linear time without using extra spac=
e.</p>
<p>If we can ensure all numbers less than the pivot are placed to the left,=
 then numbers greater than or equal to the pivot will consequently be place=
d to the right. This can be done using two pointers:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>One pointer at the left of the array (<code>lo</code>) to position the n=
umbers less than the pivot.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>One pointer to iterate through the array (<code>i</code>), looking for n=
umbers less than the pivot.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The main idea here is that whenever we encounter a number less than the =
pivot, swap it with <code>nums[lo]</code>.</p>
